{"base_rate":0.481089258698941,"brier":0.21688971255673223,"bss":0.13119835982910677,"bss_hi":0.25784430787590323,"bss_lo":-0.04589261310053855,"chart":{"base":[477.9,210.3],"fp":[166.8,139.6],"lead":"62,240.2 272,225.2 482,214.5 692,181.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.13 — higher than 19% of cities","fp":"low end -3pp, high end +26pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 37% of cities","rel":"promised 9% → rained 2%; promised 99% → rained 79%"},"rel":"118.2,456.1 416.7,363 612.5,235.6 687,126.6"},"country":"VN","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.2261875945537065,"ess":255.98193785397208,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Hue</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Hue rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>79%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 661 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 13.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.13, ranked 174 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(122&ndash;197) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>53</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>51</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>280</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Hue</b> <span class=\"muted\">Vietnam</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;48% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 48% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.13</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>122&ndash;197\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>661 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Hue &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Hue\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.33773584905661,368.2641509433962 109.46615384615384,298.0 218.86176470588236,173.23529411764707 299.46225806451616,94.32258064516128 354.02608695652174,49.6521739130435 385.34588235294115,25.137254901960773 409.18064285714286,18.0 409.18064285714286,25.80000000000001 385.34588235294115,75.0980392156863 354.02608695652174,107.68115942028987 299.46225806451616,176.51612903225805 218.86176470588236,258.88235294117646 109.46615384615384,354.0 60.33773584905661,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"206.8835098335855\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"206.8835098335855\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.33773584905661,382.0 109.46615384615384,368.0 218.86176470588236,312.4117647058824 299.46225806451616,276.3225806451613 354.02608695652174,202.63768115942028 385.34588235294115,167.88235294117646 409.18064285714286,96.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 53 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"60.33773584905661\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"109.46615384615384\" cy=\"368.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"218.86176470588236\" cy=\"312.4117647058824\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 68%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"299.46225806451616\" cy=\"276.3225806451613\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"354.02608695652174\" cy=\"202.63768115942028\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 51 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"385.34588235294115\" cy=\"167.88235294117646\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 280 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.18064285714286\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(48%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Hue the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.58) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.57).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>-0.571</td><td class='num'>40.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'>0.097</td><td class='num'>18.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>142</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.106</td><td class='num'>23.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>163</td><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'>0.581</td><td class='num'>7.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":16.4619,"lon":107.59546,"n":661,"n_cities":216,"name":"Hue","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.006603773584905661,"n":53,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.33,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.14538461538461536,"n":78,"obs":0.038461538461538464,"sig":true},{"hi":0.5800000000000003,"lo":0.33,"mean":0.4544117647058824,"n":68,"obs":0.19117647058823528,"sig":true},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.5800000000000003,"mean":0.6820967741935484,"n":62,"obs":0.2903225806451613,"sig":true},{"hi":0.89,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.836231884057971,"n":69,"obs":0.4927536231884058,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.89,"mean":0.9247058823529412,"n":51,"obs":0.5882352941176471,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9920357142857142,"n":280,"obs":0.7857142857142857,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":13.3,"provisional":false,"rank":174,"rank_hi":197.0,"rank_lo":122.0,"reliability":0.06196008428681869,"resolution":0.09394542479192042,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"hue"